# Castor EDC in Livebook

```elixir
# To use checkouts instead of the published packages, set
# CASTOR_EDC_KINO_PATH, and CASTOR_EDC_PATH for the core.
kino = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_KINO_PATH")
core = System.get_env("CASTOR_EDC_PATH")

Mix.install(
  [if(kino, do: {:ex_castor_edc_kino, path: kino}, else: {:ex_castor_edc_kino, "~> 0.1.0"})] ++
    if(core, do: [{:ex_castor_edc, path: core, override: true}], else: [])
)
```

## Introduction

This notebook connects to Castor EDC, picks a study and looks around it, without writing any setup code.
Everything here only reads: nothing in it changes the study.

Add your API credentials as Livebook secrets first, `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID` and `CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET`, in the notebook's Secrets panel (the key icon in the sidebar).
You create the credentials on your [account settings page](https://data.castoredc.com/account/settings).
The connection cell reads them from the secrets, so they never appear in the notebook.

## Connecting

Pick the server your studies are on, and test the connection.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.CastorEDC.Kino.ConnectionCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
client =
  CastorEDC.new(
    client_id: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_ID"),
    client_secret: System.fetch_env!("LB_CASTOR_EDC_CLIENT_SECRET"),
    base_url: "https://data.castoredc.com"
  )
```

## Picking a study

Once the client exists, this cell lists the studies it can reach.

